2 to the power of 10 is **1,024**.

This means 2 multiplied by itself 10 times: 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 = 1,024

Fun fact: this is why 1,024 bytes is called a kilobyte in computing, and why 2¹⁰ is such an important number in computer science!
